                <pb facs="0807" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/222: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kreeck</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-12T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9. The Department has been informally advised through the Bolivian Legation that
                    Paraguayan troops are building a fortress 30 kilometers from the Bolivian
                    fortress Sorpresa, located 1 kilometer from Chamar Lagoon. At the northwest of
                    Arce and 40 kilometers from the said point they are also building another
                    fortress called Boqueron. The Legation calls attention to the seriousness of the
                    situation which may arise through construction of these fortresses so close to
                    those of Sorpresa and Arce. Report by telegraph any information in your
                    possession regarding matter without discussing it with any officials.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
